  "S3": {
    "bottom_line_reference": "Using only the 10-K for historical base lines and the oracle assumptions for the forecast and WACC, the base-case DCF gives enterprise value of 2170873.3 and equity value of 2247212.3. Dividing equity value, not enterprise value, by diluted shares gives 91.67 per share. Across the plus/minus 50bp WACC band at the base 0.04 terminal growth rate, the fair-value range is about 86.6-97.4 per share. That is materially below the oracle market price of 206.64, implying about 55.64 downside on the base case. The conclusion is assumption-conditional, and the terminal value is a dominant contributor at 70.35 of EV.",
